{title: The Greatest of These}
{subtitle: 1 Corinthians 13}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebm/Gb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I could sing like the [Dm7]angels
[Gm]I could speak in every [Eb]tongue
[Bb]But without love I'm [Dm7]a clanging gong
[Eb]A song that's never [Ebm]sung
[Bb]I could move every [Dm7]mountain
[Gm]Give away all that [Eb]I own
[Bb]But without love I gain [Dm7]nothing
[Eb]I'm standing here a[Ebm]lone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Love is patient, [Dm7]love is kind
[Eb]Keeps no record of [Fsus4]wrongs
It bears all [Bb]things, believes all [Dm7]things
Hopes all [Eb]things, endures all [Fsus4]things
[F]Love never [Bb]ends
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When I was a child I spoke [Dm7]like a child
[Gm]Thought the way that children [Eb]do
[Bb]Now we see a dim reflection [Dm7]in a mirror
[Eb]But then face to face with [Ebm]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Love is patient, [Dm7]love is kind
[Eb]Keeps no record of [F]wrongs
It bears all [Bb]things, believes all [Dm7]things
Hopes all [Eb]things, endures all [F]things
Love never [Bb]ends [F/A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Faith and hope and love re[Eb]main
These [Bb]three, these [F]three
But the [Gm]greatest of these
The [Eb]greatest of these is [F]love [Bb][Dm7][Eb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Love never [Bb]ends [Dm7][Eb]
[F]Love never [Bb]ends
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] | [F] | ×3
